  {
   "id": "AX-03",
   "name": "Explicit, inert refusals",
   "repairs": [
    "SYS-I3",
    "SYS-I9"
   ],
   "rule": "A refused or failed command leaves every store as it was (the caller's own earlier writes included) and says why, with a code of the product's error family; a failure is never reported as success, as no rows, or as another error.",
   "formal": "outcome(cmd) = refused(code) => state' = state and code in ErrorFamily(cmd)",
   "repair_note": "Merges SYS-I3 (changes nothing) and SYS-I9 (says why), as the playbook's 'explicit, recorded refusals'. Extended: the caller's earlier writes in its own transaction are part of 'every store' (F-C0702, F-0409), and a silent drop or a misreported error class is a refusal that does not say why (F-0307, F-0817, F-C1602).",
